# .loopkit/config.env — per-project LoopKit settings (KEY=VALUE, no quotes needed)
#
# Copy to .loopkit/config.env. That file is gitignored by /loopkit:init because
# it may hold a webhook URL. Never put any other credential here: name the
# variable, set the value in your shell or secrets manager.
#
# Sourced by stop_gate.sh, test-regressions.sh, loop-next.sh, loop-watch.sh,
# morning-triage.sh, and read by notify_needs_human.py. The process environment
# wins over this file. Setting a *_CMD to an empty value SKIPS that step.

# --- the stop gate -----------------------------------------------------------
# LOOP_PRECHECK_CMD=
# LOOP_TEST_CMD=npm test
# LOOP_LINT_CMD=npm run lint
# LOOP_LINT_FALLBACK_CMD=npx eslint --max-warnings=0
# LOOP_TYPECHECK_CMD=npx tsc --noEmit
# LOOP_BUILD_CMD=npm run build
# LOOP_CODE_GLOBS=*.js *.jsx *.ts *.tsx *.mjs *.cjs *.py *.go *.rs *.java *.rb *.kt *.swift

# --- the regression diff -----------------------------------------------------
# A command that writes a jest/vitest-shaped JSON report to {report}:
# LOOP_TEST_JSON_CMD=npx vitest run --reporter=json --outputFile={report}
# Or feed any runner through a list file: test-regressions.sh --from-list FILE
# LOOP_TEST_BASELINE=state/known-test-failures.txt
# LOOP_MIN_NODE=20

# --- environment wrapper (secrets manager, value-blind) ----------------------
# Prefix for every gate command, split on spaces:
# LOOP_ENV_WRAPPER=doppler run --project my-app --config dev --

# --- GitHub ------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOOPKIT_REPO=owner/name            # default: `gh repo view`
# LOOPKIT_ISSUE_LABEL=loopkit        # issues the loop owns

# --- escalation webhook ------------------------------------------------------
# LOOPKIT_NEEDS_HUMAN_WEBHOOK=https://hooks.example.com/...   (Slack-compatible)
# LOOPKIT_WEBHOOK_FORMAT=slack       # slack | discord | generic
# LOOPKIT_PROJECT_NAME=my-app

# --- where heavy runs go -----------------------------------------------------
# Read by scripts/remote-gate.sh, which the implementer and reviewer agents are
# told to use when a verdict on the local machine has to be explained away. It
# stages a clone, rsyncs your working tree over it, and runs the suite in a
# container on that host. Leave unset to run locally.
#
# `:-` IS THE POINT for these two, and they are the only keys in this file that
# get it. Eight scripts source this file with `set -a`, so a bare
# LOOPKIT_REMOTE= would overwrite a correct exported value with nothing — a
# config key that takes a working setting away. The LOOP_* keys above are read
# as `${VAR-default}`, where an explicit empty means "skip this step" and the
# clobber is their documented contract. These have no such contract.
# LOOPKIT_REMOTE="${LOOPKIT_REMOTE:-}"          # user@host of the Linux box
# LOOPKIT_SSH_KEY="${LOOPKIT_SSH_KEY:-}"        # identity file, default ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
# LOOPKIT_IMAGE=node:22-bookworm                # container image
# LOOPKIT_REMOTE_DOCKER=1                       # 0 runs bare on the host

# --- misc --------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOOPKIT_WATCH_STATE_DIR=/tmp
# LOOPKIT_TOOLS_DIR=~/.loopkit/tools # model-checker install dir
# LOOPKIT_TRIAGE_PRECHECK=           # command run (fail-open) before a headless triage
